From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: Control ranges (6047)

body.createControlRange() and element.createControlRange() gave
E_NOTIMPL. HTML editors in older programs (mail composers, help and
CMS editors in a WebBrowser control) select an image or a table as a
control range. IHTMLControlRange is declared and implemented: add,
remove, item, length, commonParentElement, scrollIntoView, select (the
document's selection covers the elements), the query/exec commands of
the document on that selection, and Delete removing the elements
themselves. Every element answers IHTMLControlElement (IHTMLElement2's
members of those names), which add() takes.
---
